# Line-ending policy for a cross-platform repository.
#
# The CI runner and the Docker image are Linux. If `docker-entrypoint.sh` is
# checked out with CRLF, its `#!/bin/sh` shebang breaks inside the Alpine
# container, and `make` refuses a CRLF Makefile. Everything text is therefore
# normalized to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit (belt and braces) for the files where the wrong ending is fatal.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts would be the exception if they are ever added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.bundle binary
